---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/guides';
const title = 'Shopify email operator guides: choose the next decision';
const desc = 'Find the guide and working document for platform selection, rollout, migration, audience rules, offers and measurement.';
const guides = [
  { slug: 'selection-framework', name: 'Selection framework', job: 'Score Shopify email tools against your operating constraints before migration' },
  { slug: 'implementation-plan', name: 'Implementation plan', job: 'Roll out lifecycle flows in sequence without collision bugs' },
  { slug: 'migration', name: 'Migration playbook', job: 'Move lists, flows, and suppression logic between platforms with explicit cutover and recovery checks' },
  { slug: 'pricing-models', name: 'Pricing models', job: 'Model per-contact vs per-email economics at your actual send volume' },
  { slug: 'segmentation', name: 'Segmentation', job: 'Define audiences with actionable inclusion, exclusion and exit rules' },
  { slug: 'deliverability', name: 'Deliverability', job: 'Protect inbox placement while scaling lifecycle sends' },
  { slug: 'discount-discipline', name: 'Discount discipline', job: 'Stop training every shopper to wait for the next code' },
  { slug: 'consent-compliance', name: 'Consent & compliance', job: 'Audit permission provenance and selected US/UK email requirements' },
  { slug: 'revenue-attribution', name: 'Revenue attribution', job: 'Measure incremental email revenue, not rented last-click credit' },
  { slug: 'flow-collision-prevention', name: 'Flow collision prevention', job: 'Suppress overlapping automations before customers get three discounts in one day' },
  { slug: 'replenishment-tools', name: 'Replenishment tools', job: 'Choose a Shopify email tool for repeat purchase timing, education, and reorder pilots' },
];
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Which guide should I read first?",
    "answer": "Start with the live decision: selection and pricing before procurement, migration before switching senders, or the incident-specific guide when messages conflict or delivery deteriorates. Capture the current state before changing it."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do I need to read every guide before making a change?",
    "answer": "No. Read the guide for the decision and its dependencies. An offer change needs both discount economics and collision checks; a sender migration needs permission and delivery review as well as a cutover plan."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are vendor recommendations a substitute for a demonstration?",
    "answer": "No. Treat Sequenzy and other candidates as a shortlist to investigate. Require the candidate to demonstrate your actual data, eligibility and failure cases, and obtain a current written quote."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a completed reading task produce?",
    "answer": "A store-specific artifact with an owner: a scorecard, cost model, cutover map, eligibility rule, offer register or measurement plan. Record unresolved decisions and proposed checks; reading alone does not validate a workflow."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <p class="catalog-kicker">Operator handbooks</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Shopify email operator guides</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose a guide by the decision you need to make, then leave with a working document someone owns. This directory is for retention leads, founders and agency operators coordinating the email program across people and tools.</p>
    <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/selection-framework">Evaluate a platform</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/use-cases">Find a workflow playbook</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Choose a starting point</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Buying or renewing:</strong> pair <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">selection</a> with <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">pricing</a>. Produce a requirements scorecard and a cost worksheet at your own audience and send volumes. A low quote is not enough if the required workflow cannot be demonstrated.</li>
      <li><strong>Launching or changing senders:</strong> read <a class="link" href="/guides/implementation-plan">implementation</a> and, when switching, <a class="link" href="/guides/migration">migration</a>. Produce a message-owner inventory, dependency map, cutover decision and rollback owner. Review permission and delivery before expanding sends.</li>
      <li><strong>Conflicting messages or offers:</strong> pair <a class="link" href="/guides/flow-collision-prevention">collision prevention</a> with <a class="link" href="/guides/discount-discipline">discount discipline</a>. Produce a dispatch priority matrix and offer register. Message timing and checkout redemption need separate decisions.</li>
      <li><strong>Audience or performance questions:</strong> pair <a class="link" href="/guides/segmentation">segmentation</a> with <a class="link" href="/guides/revenue-attribution">attribution</a>. Define who qualifies, what changes for them and how you will distinguish credited revenue from an incremental effect.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If the immediate problem is a permission gap or delivery incident, start with the relevant guide below and investigate the affected sends before making a platform purchase. Changing software does not itself establish permission or explain missing messages.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container py-12">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black">All {guides.length} operator guides</h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">{guides.map((g) => (<a class="card group" href={`/guides/${g.slug}`}><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">{g.name}</h3><p class="mt-3">{g.job}</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm font-bold">Read guide →</p></a>))}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Turn reading into an assigned change</h2>
    <p>Use one handoff record: observed problem, affected audience, current sender, proposed change, dependency, owner, acceptance evidence and recovery action. Link the current configuration or export and date it. Keep a proposed test distinct from an executed test with captured results. If the data needed for a decision is missing, assign its collection rather than treating an example in a guide as your baseline.</p>
    <p>For a new retention hire, a useful proposed sequence is to inventory live senders and permissions first, map overlaps and active offers next, and then review audience and measurement definitions. Procurement can wait until the inventory shows a capability gap. During a migration, change that order to address cutover dependencies; an arbitrary reading calendar should not override a live operational risk.</p>
    <h2>Three proposed routing examples</h2>
    <p><strong>A bill has increased:</strong> collect billed audience counts, send volume, add-ons and renewal terms; use the pricing worksheet before deleting contacts or switching platforms. Take the resulting requirements into selection. This is a diagnostic path, not evidence that any vendor is cheaper.</p>
    <p><strong>A shopper reports two incompatible offers:</strong> preserve the messages, code terms and event history. The collision guide helps assign dispatch ownership; the discount guide helps reconcile outstanding promises and redemption rules. Do not infer an unsubscribe improvement or a revenue gain from fixing the configuration.</p>
    <p><strong>A repeat-purchase program is proposed:</strong> use replenishment to decide product eligibility and reorder context, segmentation to define the audience, and attribution to design evaluation. Subscription status and recent purchases may change eligibility. These are proposed planning examples, not merchant case studies.</p>
    <h2>Use the rest of the site for a different job</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="/use-cases">Use-case playbooks</a> focus on individual workflows. <a class="link" href="/for">Store-type pages</a> add product and audience constraints. <a class="link" href="/apps">App pages</a> and <a class="link" href="/compare">comparisons</a> help investigate suppliers after requirements are clear. Verify current capabilities and terms directly before committing; this hub does not establish a winner or certify those pages.</p>
    <p>Sequenzy may be included in a candidate demonstration alongside other tools that meet your requirements. Bring the same scenarios and evidence requests to each supplier. Keep unresolved integration, pricing, operator and jurisdiction questions in the decision record instead of assuming a recommendation resolves them.</p>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Operator guides hub FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
